template-extraction.md
# Four extraction stages

## 1. Specific source descriptions

Every original prompt, ordered solution row and every answer is retained in source.json and review.md. IDs 69061/75409 use sin/cos and a logarithmic y separation; 75408 first converts reciprocal cosine squared to secant squared; 75410 integrates x²; 75411 uses arcsin on |x|<1; 75412 uses secant on (-π/2,π/2). 235519 is the T≠25 exponential-factor blank with rate 0.03. 69062 is autonomous y²+1 and tan(x+C). 75407 integrates 3y² to y³ then real cube-root isolation. 326685 integrates e^y and x to obtain ln(x²/2+C). 332867 separates the real cube root of y², integrates y^(-2/3)/3, and cubes x²+C. All banks have five options except the one-choice blank. Original data has no unrated practice records.

## 2. Shared mathematical pattern

Separate a factorizable first-order ODE already presented as y′=h(x)g(y); integrate two elementary primitives and isolate the dependent variable as a complete local general family. Nonzero constraints survive division, poles are excluded locally, logarithm arguments are positive, cube roots are real, and even roots keep both signs. Constants C and K represent arbitrary constants rather than fixed values.

## 3. Components and complete observed banks

The eleven complete observed banks are named observed_<template>. `source-cases.json` maps every original source to a zero-translation/a=1/rate-0.03/ambient-25 recipe. Each source option has its own full equation or factor; identities are regenerated with field ownership. The source profile transforms the entire mathematical component by the same input translation. This reproduces each source value, but does not assert that the observed distractor's author intended a particular error. Such intent is underdetermined and remains unresolved. Options and their exact value strings appear together in source.json and the original replay review; no option has been discarded.

Source observations and repairs: negative_exp's ln(x²)/2+C and ln(x/2)+C give equivalent general families on x>0; ln(x²/2)+C is a different power-law family. Wrong-option domain observation: linear_sec2's K ln(tan x) is nonreal for negative x and singular at zero in the stated interval; linear_sin ln(cos x)+K also fails globally although it has local real intervals. Wrong-form observation: autonomous_tan's y=y³/3+y+C is an intentionally incorrect implicit self-referential option for the explicit-answer request; this is not a defective correct answer or defective question. Temperature's part-1 reference omits its differential equation. The negative_exp bank contains equivalent wrong options, not multiple mathematically correct options. Raw profiles preserve all observations as evidence through the public API, explicitly marked `observed_bank_anomalies_retained`. Normal generation repairs the temperature presentation by supplying the ODE and uses separately authored complete operation banks. No mathematical change is hidden inside exact fidelity totals.

Authored bank: correct inversion; use unintegrated h instead of primitive H; reverse primitive sign; omit inverse and use H+C; put the arbitrary constant outside the inverse. The exponential case uses K exp(h), K exp(-H), H+C and exp(H)+K. Tangent uses tan(a+C), tan(-ax+C), ax+C and tan(ax)+C. Its full source bank masks use ax inside tan/cot/sec; the self-referential y expression intentionally omits a as an observed omission-shaped wrong option, without claiming recovered error intent. Cube/root/log cases apply the corresponding full inverse to h+C and -H+C, retain H+C, and add C after inversion. These recipes are actual separation/integration/isolation errors. Profiles are complete and reject on any equivalent families; no first-valid pool is used.

## 4. Reusable masks and bounds

Each full math expression is extracted from dollar spans; textual commands, dy/dx, dx, function-name labels y=y(x), and prose variable labels are protected before free input symbols become a translation argument slot. Unit-derivative translations preserve every primitive, integrand and isolation row. Source h=0 (or a=1 for tangent) is processed through this normal recipe, not returned from a literal replay branch. Source bank values, full prose and row order are exactly compared separately from mathematical truth. Displayed-stage checks read the generated TeX back independently.

Easy: four observed templates, h∈[-8,8] except autonomous tan with positive a=1..5 multiplying (y²+1); translations are absorbed into C and excluded from variety. Moderate: seven observed templates, six homogeneous exponential families with h∈[-8,8] plus temperature ambient∈{15,20,25,30,35}, rate∈{.02,.03,.04,.05,.06}; only the five rates affect the assessed factor, so ambient is excluded from the blank mathematical fingerprint. Translation changes actual integrands; homogeneous temperature time shifts would be absorbed into K and are not sampled. This gives 56 easy and 107 moderate substantive peers (127 parameter presentations) across unordered families, without claiming cosmetic constant renaming as variety.

Hard canonical_root: a(x+h)^n/y, positive a=1..5, n=2..4, h∈[-4,4], x+h>0, both root signs on positive-radicand intervals. Hard intro_log: a exp(bx-y), 1≤|a|≤5, 2≤|b|≤5 with a/b>0, positive logarithm argument; signed coefficients are permitted only together, keeping the complete bank real on its natural domain. Authored logarithm and reciprocal-cube source variants use x+h>0 so their outside-inverse distractors remain real and differentiable; this is an explicit normal-bank local-domain restriction, not a raw source condition. There are 135 canonical peers and 40 coefficient peers in the second family. Hard coefficient reciprocal arithmetic and branch/domain care match the same canonical separation method; no additional integration technique is introduced. Explicit parameter dictionaries use the same guards as samplers.

Task fingerprints contain the assessed ODE and domain family; temperature blank normalizes T-ambient to y so the supplied ambient offset does not inflate assessed task variety, excluding choices/profile/order. Content identity contains version, actual prompt, fixed worked solution and sorted complete bank. Different banks change presentation identity; option shuffling does not. Family comparisons normalize logarithm/tangent/power inversions to affine primitive constants and exponentials modulo nonzero multiplicative constants.

No plot extraction or rende
